  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-2">
    <td>Iron deficiency anemia from chronic blood loss from the colon tumor</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>D50.0</td><td>S — Synthetic finding echoing the documented &apos;hemorrhage in the upper part of the intestines&apos;; no blood count from his lifetime exists.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-3">
    <td>Hemangioma of the liver, 9 mm, segment VI; incidental finding characterized by MRI, not a metastasis</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>D18.03</td><td>S — Synthetic incidental finding; it addresses, and does not confirm, the unverified suggestion of liver spread.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-4">
    <td>Acute viral upper respiratory infection during adjuvant chemotherapy, without fever or neutropenia; resolved</td><td>resolved</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>J06.9</td><td>S — Synthetic intercurrent illness at an unscheduled visit; it does not echo a documented illness.</td>
  </tr></tbody></table></text>

